# Baseline CNN: EMNIST Letters (A–Z)

This folder contains the **baseline model** for our capstone: a small convolutional neural network (CNN) trained to classify handwritten letters into 26 classes. It is the reference point that the improved CNN and the ANN/MLP are compared against.

## Dataset

- **Source:** [Voxel51/emnist-letters-tiny](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Voxel51/emnist-letters-tiny) (10,000 images in this download)
- **Task:** 26-class handwritten letter recognition (upper- and lowercase combined per letter)
- **Input:** 28×28 grayscale images, shape `(N, 28, 28, 1)`, pixel values normalized to [0, 1]
- **Labels:** integers `0 = A, 1 = B, ..., 25 = Z`

### Fixed splits (shared by all models)

| Split | Images | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `train.npz` | 6,837 | Fit model weights |
| `val.npz` | 855 | Early stopping / model selection |
| `test.npz` | 855 | Final evaluation only (run once) |

The splits are a stratified 80/10/10 split of the 8,547 source-train images, created with seed 42 during preprocessing. The baseline loads these exact files and does **not** create its own split. The original source-tagged test set (`original_test_optional.npz`, 1,453 images) only contains letters A–S, so it is not used for this evaluation.

## Model architecture

| Layer | Details |
|---|---|
| Input | 28 × 28 × 1 |
| Conv2D | 32 filters, 3×3, ReLU, same padding |
| MaxPooling2D | 2×2 |
| Conv2D | 64 filters, 3×3, ReLU, same padding |
| MaxPooling2D | 2×2 |
| Flatten | |
| Dropout | 0.3 |
| Dense | 128 units, ReLU |
| Dense (output) | 26 units, softmax |

The architecture diagram is saved as `baseline_architecture.png`.

## Training setup

- **Framework:** TensorFlow / Keras
- **Optimizer:** Adam (default learning rate)
- **Loss:** sparse categorical cross-entropy
- **Batch size:** 64
- **Max epochs:** 30 with early stopping (monitor `val_loss`, patience 5, best weights restored)
- **Random seed:** 42
- **Augmentation:** none

